{"connection_id": "BC-7efdc5d337c00cf90ab0", "ref": "WLC:Exod.17.6", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "water for a thirsty people", "note": "Water comes from the struck rock so that the people may drink. This gives a wilderness counterpart to the commentary's claim that water is what keeps communal and travelling life standing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dc6fc721c7fec08311b3", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Moses reaches Midian’s well", "note": "The commentary sends Musa on a road to Midian and then to its water; Exodus 2:15 sends fleeing Moses to Midian, where he sits by a well, supplying the same journey-to-well opening."}
{"connection_id": "BC-36c13dae0bc73acf6ce4", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Moses, Midian, well, journey", "note": "Moses flees to Midian and sits by a well, the direct narrative setting behind the commentary's Musa who reaches the water of Midian while seeking a way on his journey."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1cbe77c3224bb7e183b9", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "daughters draw water for flocks", "note": "The commentary identifies two women unable to water their herds; Exodus 2:16 has seven daughters come to draw water and fill the troughs, giving the shared well scene its Israelite form."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a563409d2c7a18f1c0f", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "daughters drawing water for flock", "note": "The verse gives the precise well-side tableau developed beside Qur'an 28:23: Midian's priest has daughters who draw water and fill troughs to water their flock; Exodus says seven where the Qur'anic scene has two."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cb3d5945ea2f8c7d4881", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.17", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Moses waters the flock", "note": "The commentary says Musa waters the women’s flocks; Exodus 2:17 has Moses rise, defend the daughters from shepherds, and water their flock."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cf5449347ea8266b3a9c", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.17", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "who makes room at the well", "note": "The commentary says the women wait for shepherds to leave and Musa then waters them; Exodus has Moses drive the shepherds off himself, shifting the aid from waiting and serving to direct intervention."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8d71fadb640b2633ff5d", "ref": "WLC:Exod.2.17", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Moses aids women and waters flock", "note": "Exodus makes Moses drive off the hostile shepherds and personally water the flock. It is the close counterpart to the commentary's two women who cannot water until the shepherds leave and are then helped by Musa."}
