{"connection_id": "BC-ee2b4897e6958d9b325c", "ref": "WLC:Jer.10.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wind, clouds, and rain in sequence", "note": "The commentary says winds move and spread clouds before rain; Jeremiah says God makes clouds rise, flashes lightning for rain, and brings wind from storehouses."}
{"connection_id": "BC-213b0c34ca006330b2b0", "ref": "WLC:Jer.14.22", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God alone gives rain", "note": "Jeremiah asks whether foreign gods or the heavens can give showers, and confesses that YHWH made all these things. This makes rain a dependent gift of the creator, closely matching the commentary's rain as mercy and benefit rather than autonomous weather."}

