{"connection_id": "BC-f68f1750fdbad6b08fa4", "ref": "WLC:Jer.2.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fountain versus broken cistern", "note": "The people abandon a fountain of living water for cracked cisterns that cannot retain water. It offers a negative well-and-storage counterpart to the commentary's gathered water and the structural devices at a well's mouth."}
