{"connection_id": "BC-e27edad7576333fbe4dd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.1", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise frames creation’s water", "note": "The commentary connects hamd with rain and the earth’s fertility; Psalm 104 begins in praise and then describes God’s care of clouds, mountains, plants, and food."}
{"connection_id": "BC-47b33459bd5f89d7e190", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "cloud chambers water mountains", "note": "The commentary describes layered clouds and rain that grows plants; Psalm 104 says God waters the mountains from the upper chambers and satisfies the earth with fruit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e3f3510a5f320441a8fd", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "watered mountains satisfy earth", "note": "God waters the mountains from his upper chambers, and the earth is satisfied with the fruit of his work. It is a close scriptural formulation of heavenly water sustaining terrestrial growth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5f8ce813859d4f853392", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "grass and plants for people", "note": "The commentary follows rain into tender plants and fields; Psalm 104 says God makes grass grow for cattle and plants for people to cultivate."}
{"connection_id": "BC-18996e74a561d9aef105", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "grass and plants grow from water", "note": "The same hymn says God causes grass to grow for cattle and plants for human cultivation. It supplies the food-and-livestock outcome that the commentary connects to rain and provision."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4e0ea756924f6e8dc71d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.104.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "food and drink from the earth", "note": "The commentary links water to livelihood and food; Psalm 104 names wine, oil, and bread as gifts that gladden, nourish, and strengthen human life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0485462872513fa38640", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.35", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "desert becomes pool and spring", "note": "The commentary says rain restores soil and makes it fruitful; Psalm 107 says God turns wilderness into a pool and parched land into springs."}
{"connection_id": "BC-60cdf19d8f52d58afebf", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.35", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "desert turned to pools and springs", "note": "God turns desert into a pool and parched ground into water springs. The reversal makes a concrete companion to rain repairing a people's condition and to water being drawn from otherwise dry ground."}
{"connection_id": "BC-44c6d1a8bcfab844638e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.36", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hungry people settle by water", "note": "The commentary moves from water to livelihood; Psalm 107 says God settles hungry people there and they establish a city to live in."}
{"connection_id": "BC-03d0077db8f0afc0089a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.37", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fields and vineyards become fruitful", "note": "The commentary follows rain into plants and food; Psalm 107 describes sowing fields, planting vineyards, and obtaining a fruitful yield."}
{"connection_id": "BC-110f15f53756ab41c6aa", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.38", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessing increases people and herds", "note": "The commentary says rain improves people’s condition and feeds animals; Psalm 107 says God blesses the people so they multiply and their livestock increase."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9bd62d483ab64a37921f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.133.2", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew na'im, pleasant", "note": "The commentary’s N-ʿ-M family describes life’s beauty and freshness; Psalm 133 calls shared life good and pleasant with Hebrew na'im, a cognate use centered on what is delightful."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7160ca970bea72c3b1f2", "ref": "WLC:Ps.135.7", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wind and rain from God’s storehouses", "note": "The commentary pairs wind, heavy cloud, and rainfall; Psalm 135 gives the same cluster as God’s work, bringing clouds, lightning for rain, and winds from storehouses."}
{"connection_id": "BC-afe1460549b459df7f43", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.11", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Spirit leads to level ground", "note": "The commentary asks for the straight way; the psalm asks God’s good Spirit to lead the speaker on level ground, a specific guidance formula."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1ec04cc917c91656b1c0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.147.7", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanksgiving beside rain and growth", "note": "The commentary places hamd beside rain and mercy; Psalm 147’s call to sing with thanksgiving leads directly into its account of clouds, rain, grass, and animal food."}
